<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02FH">Exercise <span data-tag="02FH">6.2.2.30</span>.</a> Suppose that the conditions of Corollary <a data-tag="02FG" href="/tag/02FG">6.2.2.29</a> are satisfied and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a full subcategory of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Show that $\eta $ exhibits $L$ as a $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$-reflection functor if and only if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
For each object $X \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the object $L(X)$ is contained in $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
For each object $Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}'$, there exists an isomorphism $Y \rightarrow L(X)$ for some object $X \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
<p> If the subcategory $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}' \subseteq \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is replete (Example <a data-tag="01EX" href="/tag/01EX">4.4.1.12</a>), then it is uniquely determined by these conditions. </p>
</article>
